# The rice's own Omarchy shell plugins, each published as a standalone public
# repo so `omarchy plugin add` can install it (shokupan-plugins ADR-0044
# rule 3/4). One line per plugin:
#
#   <id> <git-url>
#
# <id>       the plugin id from its manifest.json — what shell.json's bar.layout
#            and Omarchy's IPC routing use. NEVER rename these: austinkarren.*
#            ids come from `omarchy plugin clone` and are what make the clone
#            take over upstream's bar slot; shokupan.* is our third-party
#            namespace (`omarchy.*` is reserved and rejected).
# <git-url>  the plugin's own repo. `omarchy plugin add` clones the URL and
#            reads manifest.json at the REPO ROOT, which is why these are seven
#            repos and not one — see omarchy-plugin-add, and the layout note in
#            the shokupan-plugins README.
#
# The repos are named `omarchy-<function>`, the convention the plugin directory's
# own docs use, because that is what a stranger searches. The ids did not change
# with them: repo name and plugin id are deliberately different here.
#
# Development still happens in the shokupan-plugins monorepo under `plugins/`;
# these repos are the published edge. A change lands there first and is
# republished — so after editing a plugin, push the split repo too or the
# directory serves stale code.
#
# `loaf plugins` links the monorepo checkout into ~/.config/omarchy, which is
# what this machine runs. This manifest is for anyone installing them the
# public way, and for re-deriving the list after a rename.
#
# A plugin that is retired comes OFF this list and its source moves out of the
# monorepo's `plugins/` directory, into `retired/`. Both halves are needed:
# dropping the line alone leaves a shipped-but-unpublished plugin, which
# `loaf plugins --index` calls red, and moving the source alone leaves a
# published repo this monorepo no longer backs. `shokupan.notifications` was
# retired that way on 2026-08-24 — see shokupan-plugins ADR-0044's addendum for
# why.

